Rule 1 (operands must be broadcastable along all axes)
{v_1 : tensor, v_2 : tensor} |= ∀ i ∈ [0, (if ndim(v_1) ≥ ndim(v_2) then ndim(v_1) else ndim(v_2)) - 1] : ((if i < ndim(v_1) then shape(v_1, ndim(v_1) - 1 - i) else 1) = (if i < ndim(v_2) then shape(v_2, ndim(v_2) - 1 - i) else 1)) ∨ (if i < ndim(v_1) then shape(v_1, ndim(v_1) - 1 - i) else 1) = 1 ∨ (if i < ndim(v_2) then shape(v_2, ndim(v_2) - 1 - i) else 1) = 1
>>
Rule 2 (each input tensor has non-negative dimensions)
{v_1 : tensor, v_2 : tensor} |= ∀ i ∈ [0, ndim(v_1) - 1] : shape(v_1, i) ≥ 0 ∧ ∀ j ∈ [0, ndim(v_2) - 1] : shape(v_2, j) ≥ 0
>>
Rule 3 (min/max are well-defined for non-empty inputs)
{v_1 : tensor, v_2 : tensor} |= (if (∀ i ∈ [0, ndim(v_1) - 1] : shape(v_1, i) > 0) then min(v_1) ≤ max(v_1)) ∧ (if (∀ j ∈ [0, ndim(v_2) - 1] : shape(v_2, j) > 0) then min(v_2) ≤ max(v_2))
>>
Rule 4 (zero-sized dimensions are compatible with broadcasting)
{v_1 : tensor, v_2 : tensor} |= ∀ i ∈ [0, (if ndim(v_1) ≥ ndim(v_2) then ndim(v_1) else ndim(v_2)) - 1] : (if ((if i < ndim(v_1) then shape(v_1, ndim(v_1) - 1 - i) else 1) = 0) then (((if i < ndim(v_2) then shape(v_2, ndim(v_2) - 1 - i) else 1) = 0) ∨ ((if i < ndim(v_2) then shape(v_2, ndim(v_2) - 1 - i) else 1) = 1))) ∧ (if ((if i < ndim(v_2) then shape(v_2, ndim(v_2) - 1 - i) else 1) = 0) then (((if i < ndim(v_1) then shape(v_1, ndim(v_1) - 1 - i) else 1) = 0) ∨ ((if i < ndim(v_1) then shape(v_1, ndim(v_1) - 1 - i) else 1) = 1)))
>>
Rule 5 (dtype is well-defined for both operands)
{v_1 : tensor, v_2 : tensor} |= dtype_(v_1) = dtype_(v_1) ∧ dtype_(v_2) = dtype_(v_2)
